  "comments": "Obverse engraver initials varieties exist:<br />\r\n1970-83 - &#039;T.S.&#039; below base of Coat of Arms right hand side (Tommy Sasseen).<br />\r\n1984 - no engraver initials (Arthur Sutherland).<br />\r\n1985-89 - &#039;A L S&#039; below base of Coat of Arms left hand side (Arthur Sutherland).<br /><br /><br />\r\nReverse with Royal Protea flower was in use from 1965 till 1990 and is known in 2 types.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span> - digits in 20 connect with slits in 0 for tail of 2, pentels above 20 with midribs.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span> - digits in 20 connect with tail of 2 over 0, pentels above 20 narrow and without midribs.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/617b116d3cb0a.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/617b116d3cb0a.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"160\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Combinations</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span>: 1965-1969 all issues, 1970 MS (?).<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>: 1970 MS, 1970 PS, 1971-1990 all issues.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Abbreviations</span><br />\r\nMS - mint set, PS - proof set.",
